# What reaches the MCP function's deployment, as an allowlist: ignore
# everything, then let through only what `api/index.py` needs. `.gitignore`
# keeps personal data out of git; this is the separate question of what
# reaches Vercel on a CLI deploy, and a blocklist here kept missing things
# (web/.env.local, data/wrapped_private/, data/wrapped_report.json).
#
# No data ships at all. The function downloads the coarse deploy warehouse
# from a private Blob store on cold start (selector.mcp.deploy_data), so a
# Git deploy and a CLI deploy produce the same thing. See docs/DEPLOY_MCP.md.
#
# pyproject.toml stays out on purpose: Vercel's Python builder prefers
# `uv sync` against it over `pip install -r requirements.txt`, and its
# dependency list is the full local dev set (librosa, torch, ...), which
# blew the 500MB bundle limit on the first deploy.
#
# .git is let through because Vercel applies this file to Git deployments
# too, and vercel.json's ignoreCommand needs the history to `git diff` the
# pushed commit. Without it, every push to main built regardless of what
# changed. The history is the public repo's, so nothing private rides along.

/*
!/api
!/src
!/requirements.txt
!/vercel.json
!/.git

__pycache__/
*.pyc
